  ('cortina-dampezzo-italy', '02F', 'Cortina d''Ampezzo', 'Italy', 'The Queen of the Dolomites', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'Italian Alps / Dolomites', '{"culture","hiking","romance","ski","sports","ultra"}', '{"alpine","refined","dramatic"}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'anchor', '{"key_facts":["Two-time Winter Olympic host: 1956 (first televised Winter Games) + Milano-Cortina 2026 (held 6-22 Feb 2026); Queen of the Dolomites at ~1,224 m","Hosted at 2026 Games: women''s Alpine (Tofane), bob/skeleton/luge (new Cortina Sliding Centre), curling (Cortina Curling Olympic Stadium)","Cortina ski area: 120 km slopes (45 easy/59 intermediate/16 difficult), 25 lifts, 1,217-2,828 m; Tofana/Faloria/Cristallo/Cinque Torri","Dolomiti Superski: 1,246 km slopes, 450 lifts, 12 resorts on one pass - largest ski area in the world; Sellaronda circuit 44 km","Freccia nel Cielo cable car to Tofana di Mezzo 3,244 m (3rd-highest Dolomite peak); winter season ~5 Dec 2025-12 Apr 2026","Olympia delle Tofane classic women''s World Cup downhill course (run each January; used for 2026 Olympic women''s Alpine)","Dolomites UNESCO World Heritage since 26 Jun 2009 (142,000 ha, 9 mountain systems); Ladin culture of the Ampezzo valley","Lagazuoi (Falzarego to ~2,800 m in 3 min) + Cinque Torri open-air WWI museums - largest in the Dolomites (~5 km of restored front line)","Five-star hotels: Cristallo (Luxury Collection, 74 rooms), Grand Hotel Savoia (Radisson Collection, 132 rooms), Rosapetra (SLH, 33 rooms)","Dolomiti Superski adult day pass ~EUR 77-86 (2025/26); adult season ~EUR 870; ~2.5 hrs by road from Venice"],"safety":{"emergency":"112 (single European emergency) / 118 medical + Soccorso Alpino mountain rescue / 115 fire","hospital":"Ospedale Codivilla-Putti, Cortina (Via Codivilla; tel 0436 883111; emergency point, upgraded for 2026 Games); trauma transfer Belluno/Treviso often by helicopter","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","activity_n